 "notes_path": "history/polities/_notes/eu-11-x.md",
 "problems": [
  "Cliopatria's Kingdom of England shapes (936-1707) and the Great Britain and UK rows contain Irish land that the lordship-of-ireland and kingdom-of-ireland keyframes now draw from named Irish regions; the compiler should let the new keyframes override the England shapes on the island. earldom-of-desmond and earldom-of-ulster (other parts) use kingdom-of-england as predecessor, but the legal predecessor is lordship-of-ireland.",
  "kingdom-of-scotland (other part) has a vassal pair 1294-1493 whose counterpart is the string 'Lordship of the Isles' and a 1472 gain of Orkney and Shetland; old-kingdom-of-norway has Orkney, Shetland and Caithness-Sutherland as an 875 gain. The new lordship-of-the-isles (1336-1493) and earldom-of-orkney (872-1472) overlap those; the compiler must choose one tint per year and map the string to the slug.",
  "Slug aliases: ulaid (eu-11-i asked for kingdom-of-ulaid), kingdom-of-elmet (others used elmet), deheubarth (others used kingdom-of-deheubarth). The Gwynedd and Powys dossiers name kingdom-of-seisyllwg as Hywel Dda's realm in 942-950; the Deheubarth page says Deheubarth. Gwynedd's vassal dates for Deheubarth (1259-1277) disagree with the Deheubarth page's 1234-1283.",
  "kingdom-of-seisyllwg is a Cliopatria row (878-959) owned by another eu-11 part; deheubarth (920-1283) overlaps it in 920-959. I wrote a Seisyllwg dossier by mistake and deleted it before finishing.",
  "ulaid.json has a 700 loss of all Ulster west of the Bann to airgialla (confidence 1); the Airgialla page does not describe it and most of that land is Cenel nEogain's (tir-eoghain). Airgialla records a 1189 Louth loss to lordship-of-ireland (confidence 1) with no matching gain there. kingdom-of-ireland has a 1603 Ulster gain while tir-eoghain ends 1607.",
  "Start years of the Irish kingdoms (Leinster, Munster, Meath, Ulaid at 400; Connacht at 450; Kingdom of Elmet 450; Galloway 1000) are rounded bridges at confidence 1; Airgialla starts 450 instead of the infobox 331 to avoid overlapping Ulaid.",
  "Pages without an infobox in the WebFetch summary: Lordship of Galloway, Galloway, Lordship of the Isles; their dates come from the text. The Glyndwr Rising article could not be opened twice (url_not_found).",
  "Coordinate circles stand for places missing from the gazetteer (Skye, Kintyre, Knapdale, Mull, Lewis, Ross, Inishowen, Sycharth); a few edges are not clean (the Islay circle reaches Kintyre, the seaboard circle the south of Skye, the Ross circle the Inverness margin).",
  "Counts: 23 dossiers, 142 events, 71 source entries (every one validated with and without --resolve, 0 warnings). fixes_applied is an approximate count of validator errors fixed after first writes (ledger order, certainty reaching the end year, single-member unions, a syntax slip)."
 ],
